 same speed as when they  first turned into zombies anyone  every movie seems to have its own origin  for the zombie plague if they bother to  explain it at all  but none of them try to answer the most  basic question what exactly goes on in  these zombies heads when it comes to  brain function there's absolutely no  consistency in the world of these cold  clammy bloodthirsty creeps some zombies  move with superhuman speed and are  capable of effortlessly lifting people  into the air with their bare hands  meanwhile other zombies are seemingly  incapable of even taking a brisk  afternoon stroll for every goal-oriented  zombie with Drive and determination  [Music]  there's a whole mess of zero ambition  zombies who can barely keep it together  no dreams no ambition  [Music]  this raises more puzzling questions what  level of brain function do these undead  shambling nightmares operate on are some  zombies smarter than others and if these  zombies are technically dead how do they  have any brain function in the first  place any insights sorry here's  something else that really bugs us some  zombies have the wherewithal to be fast  as hell bounding about like young  gazelles other times they're just  shuffling along slow as snails and twice  as slimy like these boring zombies if  there really are a few rudimentary  thoughts still floating around inside  these zombie brains where exactly is the  line drawn do all the same rules apply  to mean-spirited zombie monkeys what  about majestic zombie horses  some zombies are apparently Mensa  material remember that scene in World  War Z when the undead hordes built a  towering zombie ladder to scale the wall  yeah that's not the kind of thing you  could just build on pure instinct even  for a zombie movie that type of behavior  is kind of a stretch here's something  else about zombies that we're just  supposed to accept because we're never  given any kind of rational explanation  at all  why do zombies always want to eat human  beings it's so excessive we're not  talking about some desperate compromise  made in order to survive on a lifeboat  not the zombies don't like to go on a  sailing expedition every once in a while  when it comes to zombies and their love  of human flesh we're talking about a  culinary preference like no other  whenever someone turns into a zombie it  usually only takes a matter of seconds  before they start munching on the  nearest person they can find  why do zombies like human flesh and not  say fast food Walker in a moment of  weakness why can't your standard grade  zombie just engulf a bag of Cool Ranch  Doritos like everybody else frankly this  unending quest for fresh human flesh  gets to be rather OneNote and what's  worse these unstoppable killing machines  are often willing to devour the nearest  member of their family in the name of a  good old-fashioned blood meal  enough is enough can we please get some  concrete answers as to what makes these  unspeakable monstrosity stick  [Music]  apparently when humans die and become  zombies their first instinct is to  gather in herds at least that's the  takeaway from pretty much every show  about these grim ungodly ghouls sure  there's still the occasional solo  zombies straggler that pops up from time  to time that's usually just for the sake  of a jump scare the really serious  threat arrives when a gigantic group of  zombie deadbeats stumbles onto the scene  [Applause]  whether we're talking about an intimate  group of like-minded zombies gathering  in a safe environment or a mega herd of  zombies come to eat everyone's brains  this very instant the burning question  remains the same why is this supposed to  be the natural behavior of zombies in  the first place  they're not getting more food this way  just look at them they're going to be  hungry all the time if they insist on  traveling in these kinds of numbers  because zombies are greedy and selfish  weird  whether it's the creatures and I am  Legend or those horrific monsters in  Zombieland these creatures almost always  have come to a herd mentality not that  anyone ever really bothers to explain  why the closest we ever get to a  concrete answer is this for a moment  let's turn our attention from the undead  to the living at their root zombies are  a bona fide medical curiosity that cause  uncontrollable outbreaks and exhibit  horrific symptoms that worsen over time  some shows like The Walking Dead never  confront the quarantine issue by making  the zombie virus some sort of blanket  sickness that everyone eventually tracks  but more often than not containing and  controlling the outbreak is the core  plot point in a zombie film take the  movie quarantine for example so here's a  question if a zombie outbreak affects  continents and eventually the entire  globe what happens to the people who  live on remote islands sure it's easy to  rule out the bigger players like Great  Britain after all the film 28 days later  takes place on that particular island  nation but what about smaller more  out-of-the-way locations like that  faraway Island in the life-affirming ly  awful film House of the Dead does Hawaii  remain an island paradise or does  everybody who live there also get  infected in the event of a zombie virus  outbreak  what about Madagascar is this cute  little guy gonna get turned into a  zombie  often times a zombie outbreak is  shrouded in secrecy at the beginning of  the story in order to ratchet up the  tension the protagonist is often left  completely in the dark regarding the  increasingly undead state of the world  around him or her sometimes it seems  like the zombie apocalypse took place  while a healthy chunk of the world was  getting some good old-fashioned shut-eye  sure that totally works for zombie  stories that came out before social  media was a thing but films and  television shows that take place after  the rise of Mark Zuckerberg needs to  start taking Facebook into account let's  get real here what if this woman was  loitering around your neighborhood  imagine if these ghouls spontaneously  erupted from the soil of your local  cemetery wouldn't someone try capturing  these precious moments on their  smartphone wouldn't a few folks decide  to share the spectacular sites on  Instagram what we're trying to say here  is the idea of a zombie apocalypse that  isn't thoroughly trumpeted on social  media is patently absurd not to mention  totally unrealistic here's another  aspect of zombie anatomy that's hard for  us to wrap our heads around they  basically live off of nothing all the  time and seemingly forever but even  after they've just enjoyed some human  flesh they still act like they're  totally starving they even act that way  after a gosh-darned bonafide feeding  frenzy like all these zombies literally  just ate  this zombie didn't even finish eating  the nice old lady and now he's making  moves on this other dude such a waste  what we've learned from all of this is  that zombies are basically impossible to  satisfy is there any rhyme or reason to  this zombie bloodlust let's think  rationally about it for a second if 80  or 90% of the population are turned into  zombies it makes sense that fresh human  flesh would be a hot commodity indeed  but a few years down the line it would  be nearly impossible for these zombies  to find any food to shovel into their  bellies they evidently don't need to eat  people in order to survive they're dead  so why are they always so pumped to be  eating everybody anyway and yet there  they go  skulking around in search of another  bite but if zombies are willing to snack  on the occasional dead deer like this  gentleman here why the obsession with  eating people and after they've chopped  on an unlucky human do zombies ever  crave something ice-cold and refreshing  to wash it all down with you can see the  problem here these guys must be  extremely dehydrated once again the  question of nutrition becomes  particularly sticky with long-running  shows like The Walking Dead all these  years later  how are the walkers even moving at this  point we're all familiar with the site  of a bloody zombie in fact no one even  bats an eye at the site anymore  but what about all those uninfected  people who accidentally get covered in  zombie blood The Walking Dead literally  has their heroes cover themselves in  zombie guts to sneak through the undead  zombie gridlock undetected how on earth  is that safe we know that a zombie bite  is almost always fatal and will almost  definitely turn you into a zombie even a  zombie scratch can become a health  hazard mock wait  so how and why is it okay to be covered  in fresh zombie blood why don't those  humans get infected they're bound to  have a little scratch on them somewhere  with the zombie blood to get in right in  the end it's never going to make total  sense these are all just movies about  silly made-up monsters check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  stuff are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

